$ weave threads follow --help
Follow an open thread as it goes, without being one of its clients: the agent's reply as text, or with --json its journal events (`thread/event`) as JSON lines

Usage: weave threads follow [OPTIONS] <THREAD_ID>

Arguments:
  <THREAD_ID>
          

Options:
      --turn <TURN_ID>
          Follow this turn, as `threads prompt` or `run --detach` named it, from its start to its end, exiting as `weave run` does for it; one that has ended prints at once

      --after <SEQ>
          Start after this position in its journal rather than with what happens next

      --until-turn-ends
          Stop when a turn ends, exiting as `weave run` does for it: the next turn to start, or without --after, the one running now

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Stop waiting after this long, exiting 8; the turn goes on. Seconds, or with a unit: 500ms, 90s, 5m, 2h

      --keep-waiting
          Wait on while the turn waits on a person to answer it, rather than exiting 7

      --json
          Print its journal events as JSON lines

      --host <HOST>
          The threads of another of your Hosts, by its id or name as `weave hosts` lists them, through the Dispatcher

  -h, --help
          Print help

