$ weave worktrees --help
Git worktrees: what worktrunk asks the weave Host before it removes one

Usage: weave worktrees <COMMAND>

Commands:
  pre-remove    Before a worktree is removed: fail while a thread in it runs a turn or waits on you, otherwise close its threads. worktrunk runs it as a pre-remove hook in the worktree it removes (`weave worktrees install-hook`)
  install-hook  Have worktrunk ask the weave Host before it removes a worktree: adds `weave worktrees pre-remove` to the pre-remove hooks in worktrunk's user config
  help          Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave worktrees pre-remove --help
Before a worktree is removed: fail while a thread in it runs a turn or waits on you, otherwise close its threads. worktrunk runs it as a pre-remove hook in the worktree it removes (`weave worktrees install-hook`)

Usage: weave worktrees pre-remove [PATH]

Arguments:
  [PATH]
          The worktree; the current directory when absent

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave worktrees install-hook --help
Have worktrunk ask the weave Host before it removes a worktree: adds `weave worktrees pre-remove` to the pre-remove hooks in worktrunk's user config

Usage: weave worktrees install-hook [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <CONFIG>
          worktrunk's user config. Defaults to $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/worktrunk/config.toml, else ~/.config/worktrunk/config.toml

  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave daemon --help
Manage the weave Host, which runs agents so their threads outlive the TUI

Usage: weave daemon [COMMAND]

Commands:
  run        Serve in the foreground until stopped (for launchd or systemd, or to watch its log)
  start      Start the Host in the background, if it isn't running
  stop       Stop the Host and its agents once running turns end. Threads it had open can be reopened later
  restart    Stop the Host if it's running, once running turns end, then start it again: after rebuilding weave
  status     What the Host is running (the default)
  install    Run the Host as a service (launchd's on macOS, systemd's on Linux): kept running, with no idle exit
  uninstall  Remove the service `install` wrote, stopping the Host
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave daemon run --help
Serve in the foreground until stopped (for launchd or systemd, or to watch its log)

Usage: weave daemon run [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --idle-exit <SECONDS>
          Exit after this many seconds with no threads open and no clients connected

      --config <CONFIG>
          The config file agents and MCP servers come from. Defaults to ~/.config/weave/config.toml

  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave daemon start --help
Start the Host in the background, if it isn't running

Usage: weave daemon start

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help

