$ weave dispatcher --help
The Dispatcher, which starts work on your Hosts while you're away: run, start, stop or install it, or pair this computer with it where it runs on another

Usage: weave dispatcher [COMMAND]

Commands:
  run         Run the Dispatcher in the foreground until stopped (for launchd or systemd, or to watch its log)
  start       Start the Dispatcher in the background, if it isn't running
  stop        Stop the Dispatcher. Nothing runs on schedule until it starts again; then each schedule catches up as its `--missed` says
  restart     Stop the Dispatcher if it's running, then start it again: after rebuilding weave
  status      Whether the Dispatcher runs, and how it reaches its Hosts (the default)
  install     Have launchd or systemd run the Dispatcher, from login or boot, and restart it if it stops
  uninstall   Stop the Dispatcher's service and remove it
  pair        Show a code another of your computers pairs with the Dispatcher with, and wait for it (`weave dispatcher connect` there runs this over SSH)
  devices     List the computers paired with the Dispatcher, or revoke one
  connect     Pair this computer with the Dispatcher on another, over SSH (`weave dispatcher connect homelab`) or with the URL and code `weave dispatcher pair` shows there, and offer to have this computer's Host join the Dispatcher
  disconnect  Forget the Dispatcher this computer is paired with
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave dispatcher run --help
Run the Dispatcher in the foreground until stopped (for launchd or systemd, or to watch its log)

Usage: weave dispatcher run

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave dispatcher start --help
Start the Dispatcher in the background, if it isn't running

Usage: weave dispatcher start

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help

