$ weave dispatcher pair --help
Show a code another of your computers pairs with the Dispatcher with, and wait for it (`weave dispatcher connect` there runs this over SSH)

Usage: weave dispatcher pair [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --name <NAME>
          What the Dispatcher calls the computer, instead of the name it gives

      --json
          Print the URL and code as JSON, and don't wait: for `weave dispatcher connect` on another computer, which runs this over SSH

  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave dispatcher devices --help
List the computers paired with the Dispatcher, or revoke one

Usage: weave dispatcher devices [COMMAND]

Commands:
  list    List the computers paired with the Dispatcher (the default)
  revoke  Forget a computer and close its connections. It has to pair again
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave dispatcher devices list --help
List the computers paired with the Dispatcher (the default)

Usage: weave dispatcher devices list [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --json
          Print them as JSON

  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave dispatcher devices revoke --help
Forget a computer and close its connections. It has to pair again

Usage: weave dispatcher devices revoke <DEVICE_ID>

Arguments:
  <DEVICE_ID>
          The computer's device id, as `weave dispatcher devices` lists it

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave dispatcher connect --help
Pair this computer with the Dispatcher on another, over SSH (`weave dispatcher connect homelab`) or with the URL and code `weave dispatcher pair` shows there, and offer to have this computer's Host join the Dispatcher

Usage: weave dispatcher connect [OPTIONS] <DISPATCHER> [CODE]

Arguments:
  <DISPATCHER>
          The computer SSH reaches the Dispatcher on, or the URL `weave dispatcher pair` shows there

  [CODE]
          The code `weave dispatcher pair` shows there, after its URL

Options:
      --name <NAME>
          What the Dispatcher calls this computer, and its Host; its name by default

      --host
          Have this computer's Host join the Dispatcher too, so it starts work here, without asking

      --no-host
          Leave this computer's Host alone, without asking

  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave dispatcher disconnect --help
Forget the Dispatcher this computer is paired with

Usage: weave dispatcher disconnect

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help
